  "principle": "Attached-growth on fixed media: wastewater trickles over rock or plastic media colonised by biofilm; air drawn through by natural or forced ventilation supplies oxygen; a secondary clarifier with recirculation settles sloughed biomass. RBCs rotate partially submerged discs in the flow for the same biofilm effect with low power demand.",
  "process_steps": [
    {
      "id": "PRIM",
      "name": "Primary settlement",
      "equipment": [
        "primary clarifier"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "TF",
      "name": "Trickling filter bed",
      "equipment": [
        "rock or plastic media (2-10 m deep)",
        "rotary distributor",
        "ventilation"
      ],
      "to": [
        "SEC"
      ],
      "streams": {
        "SEC": "biofilm-treated flow"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "SEC",
      "name": "Secondary clarification",
      "equipment": [
        "humus tank"
      ],
      "to": [
        "REC",
        "OUT"
      ],
      "streams": {
        "OUT": "treated effluent",
        "REC": "sloughed biomass"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "REC",
      "name": "Recirculation and sludge",
      "equipment": [
        "recirculation pumps",
        "humus sludge wasting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "OUT",
      "name": "Effluent out",
      "equipment": [
        "disinfection"
      ]
    }
  ],
